aegis-firewall (1.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * aegis-route: persist IP/CIDR custom routes to /etc/aegis/routes.d/ip.list and
    re-apply them on every ruleset (re)load, so split-tunnel routes now survive
    mode switches and reboots (they used to vanish on the next `flush ruleset`).
  * Add aegis-tor-port: restrict Tor's outbound relay port(s) via
    ReachableAddresses — like choosing a VPN port (e.g. 443 on locked-down nets).
  * Add aegis-newnym + aegis-reroute (+ aegis-reroute.service/.timer): request a
    new Tor circuit on demand, or automatically every N seconds for as long as
    the user wants (the timer stays disabled until the Tor GUI turns it on).

 -- Aegis OS <aegis@aegis-os.localdomain>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:49:24 +0000

aegis-firewall (1.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: aegis-firewall, the nftables Tor ruleset and the
    aegis-netmode service, moved out of the live-build hooks. Binary now lives
    at /usr/sbin/aegis-firewall and reads /etc/aegis/nftables-tor.conf.
  * Add aegis-netmode-set: persist + apply a network mode in one privileged
    step (invoked via pkexec from the Aegis Control Center).
  * FIX Tor browsing: the old blanket LAN bypass (10.0.0.0/8) swallowed Tor's
    AutomapHostsOnResolve range (10.192.0.0/10), so resolved sites went out
    direct and nothing loaded. Route everything through Tor instead; no LAN bypass.
  * Split-tunnel: nftables bypass sets (bypass4/bypass6) + the aegis-clearnet
    group, with aegis-route (exclude IPs) and aegis-run-clearnet (run an app
    outside the tunnel). postinst creates the aegis-clearnet group (gid 700).
  * I2P "everything" mode: fail-closed ruleset (nftables-i2p.conf) where only
    i2pd egresses, plus a system HTTP-proxy drop-in to the I2P proxy.
  * VPN: aegis-vpn imports/controls WireGuard (.conf) and OpenVPN (.ovpn); a new
    'vpn' firewall mode is a kill-switch (only the tunnel + handshake egress).
  * Split-tunnel by SITE: aegis-route-domain uses an opt-in local dnsmasq to
    resolve chosen domains to real IPs (pinned direct) while everything else
    still resolves through Tor.
  * aegis-tor-bridges manages obfs4/meek bridges; torrc gains a control port so
    the Control Center can show live bootstrap progress and request new circuits.

 -- Aegis OS <aegis@aegis-os.localdomain>  Sat, 01 Nov 2026 09:40:00 +0000
